**How to implement.** The study view's last flow step, Publish: the chosen fit run's calibration previewed and published, and its fitted materials and black boxes promoted to the library (001 §L 'Publishing: item → next revision (`Calibrated`); material or black-box object → Promote to library'; 001 §O 'a left flow strip: … → Results → Publish'; 001 §P `PublishCalibration`, `PromoteToLibrary`; .spec-md §10.5: an action that changes user-visible state names its undo or why it has none). The buttons send the window's messages (step 413), and the preview is the pure `calibratedItemsWith` (step 406), so what is shown is what is published. Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.5. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`: `ConstructorFlowStep` gains `PublishFlowStep` after `ResultsFlowStep`, its `caption` `Publish` and its `flowUiId` `flowPublishStep`, one of the study's steps (step 414); `all` now lists Items, Setups, Experiments, Data, Unknowns, Fit, Results and Publish, where S14.2 inserts Plan between Unknowns and Fit. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs`, a group after the Results step's under `// --- The study's Publish step (StudyPublishView). ---`, each with a one-line doc: `flowPublishStep` (`"FlowPublishStep"`), `studyPublishPanel` (`"StudyPublishPanel"`), `publishCalibrationPreview` (`"PublishCalibrationPreview"`), `publishCalibrationButton` (`"PublishCalibrationButton"`) and `promotionList` (`"PromotionList"`). `ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs`: `promoteButton (subject : PromotionSubject)` (step 407) is `Promote_<the material's GUID>_v<n>` or `Promote_<the item's GUID>`. (3) New `OpticalConstructor.Ui/StudyPublishView.fs`, `module OpticalConstructor.Ui.StudyPublishView`, compiled directly after `StudyResultsView.fs` (step 417): one `<Compile>` line and no comment. `studyPublishView (model) (dispatch) : IView`, its doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.5: a `ScrollViewer` scrolling both ways around a vertical `StackPanel` carrying `studyPublishPanel`, margin 8, holding `StudyUnknownsView.studyBarView` and, for `model.selectedFitRunOpt` (step 417) of the chosen study: `Fit run <name>`; the semi-bold `Publish calibration`; a vertical `StackPanel` carrying `publishCalibrationPreview` showing `study.calibratedItemsWith run model.kitItems`: for `Ok items` one line per item, `<label> → revision <n>: <name> = <value> ± <σ>, …` of its published parameters, and for `Error e` its `describe` in `MaterialsWindowView.messageColor`; `Publish calibration` (`publishCalibrationButton`, an `actionButton` on `positiveBackground`), present only when the preview is `Ok` and writes are offered (`model.kitWrites`, step 185), sending `PublishCalibration run.name`; and the line `Publishing writes each item's next revision; the values it replaces stay in the item's revision history.` (no undo is needed: the history keeps them, step 235). Then the semi-bold `Promote to library` and a vertical `StackPanel` carrying `promotionList`, one row per `run.promotionSubjectsWith study model.kitItems model.tryItemModelChoice` (step 407): `<the material's name> v<n> → its next library version` or `<the item's label> (black box) → a custom-Mueller polarizer`, with, while writes are offered, `Promote` (`promoteButton` of the subject, an `actionButton` on `positiveBackground`) sending `PromoteToLibrary (run.name, subject)`; or the line `This fit run fitted no material or black box.`; and the line `Promoting mints a new library version under the fit's provenance; the version the study opened stays as it is.` (nothing is replaced, step 408). `kitStatus` tells each outcome through the study bar (step 414). Without a fit run the panel ends with `No fit run yet: run the fit in the Fit step.`. (4) `KitWindowView.fs`: `PublishFlowStep` shows `StudyPublishView.studyPublishView model dispatch` keyed `publish`. Tests. `StudyViewTests`: `the study view UiIds are the stable intent-named ids` also pins the Publish step's ids and `promoteButton` of each subject case; without a trait, `the Publish step previews the chosen run's calibration and lists what it can promote`: over `studyKitIn` with a test-local fit run of `QZ-LR` named `QZ-LR@20261101T120000Z`, written through `writeFitRun`, fitting CPL1's `c2.retardance` at 1.55 with σ 0.002 (`ItemOwner`), on `PublishFlowStep` the preview reads `CPL1 → revision 2: c2.retardance = 1.55 ± 0.002`, `publishCalibrationButton` is present, and `promotionList` reads `This fit run fitted no material or black box.`; with a QZ black-box item fitted by a second run and chosen through `SelectFitRun`, the list holds QZ's `promoteButton`. With trait `ui-smoke`, `pressing Publish calibration writes the calibrated items' next revisions into the kit`: pressing `flowPublishStep` and `publishCalibrationButton` leaves `CPL1.item-json` at revision 2 holding the calibration and `studyStatusLine` reading `Published the calibration of CPL1 from QZ-LR@20261101T120000Z.`. `KitWindowTests`: `the flow strip UiIds are the stable intent-named ids` also pins `FlowPublishStep`; `the flow strip shows Items, Setups and Experiments left of the surface its step shows` also finds the Publish box below Results and, on `PublishFlowStep`, `studyPublishPanel`; `a read-only window withholds every write control` finds in `studyPublishView` over the read-only model neither `publishCalibrationButton` nor any `promoteButton`. `KitWindowModelTests`: `the flow strip's steps follow 001's order and a window opens on Setups` lists the eight steps with their captions; `the Data step is the Inverse constructor's alone, and leaving the Inverse constructor leaves it` also finds `stepsOf ForwardConstructor` without Publish. `ScrollExtentTests` gains `the kit window's Publish step leaves everything reachable`: `assertReachable "KitWindowPublish"` over `kitWindowView` on `PublishFlowStep` over a run calibrating three items and promoting a material and a black box. All choice construction and matching in this step MUST use step 216's payloads, including the resolved ItemModelVersion for source, ideal-polarizer and stack choices. Fixtures MUST obtain those versions from step 210's shipped model entries; runtime resolution MUST use the stored version through ItemModelProxy, never manufacture a model or use a preset/sample as the model. Existing parameter values and optical results MUST be preserved.

**Acceptance.** After the Publish step lands, the Inverse constructor's flow strip MUST end with Publish after Results, and `studyPublishView` MUST preview the chosen fit run's calibration through `calibratedItemsWith`, offer Publish calibration and one Promote per subject `promotionSubjectsWith` lists, sending `PublishCalibration` and `PromoteToLibrary`, withheld under a read-only kit; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including the changed `the flow strip's steps follow 001's order and a window opens on Setups` and `the Data step is the Inverse constructor's alone, and leaving the Inverse constructor leaves it`; ui-smoke MUST pass, including `pressing Publish calibration writes the calibrated items' next revisions into the kit`, the count rising by 1; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `the Publish step previews the chosen run's calibration and lists what it can promote` and `the kit window's Publish step leaves everything reachable`, the count rising by 2, and the changed `the study view UiIds are the stable intent-named ids`, `the flow strip UiIds are the stable intent-named ids`, `the flow strip shows Items, Setups and Experiments left of the surface its step shows` and `a read-only window withholds every write control`; and build, elevation and the twenty s40 invariants MUST pass.
